wcl_fast_power.patch (2nd version, build fix 1), against laobamac/itlwm 7204c69 (AirportItlwm 2.4.0, Tahoe/WCL build)

Why: on Wi-Fi power-on (menu, networksetup, ifconfig) and on wake, airportd
reaches the network about 10 s late. airportd (macOS 26.7.3, 25G342) starts
an auto-join with trigger power_on when POWER_CHANGED (power on) arrives while
its node still has isDriverAvailable=1 (airportdProcessDriverEvent). 7204c69
reports every power-off as "driver unavailable" and every power-on as an
interface reset plus "driver available", so airportd instead runs its chip-reset
path (-[CWXPCInterfaceContext processDriverAvailabilityForAutojoin]). With the
screen unlocked and a recently joined network without 2.4 GHz presence, that
path picks trigger auto_instant_hotspot: 5 s of Instant Hotspot browsing, then
the retry interval (5 or 10 s), before known networks are scanned.

What:
1. Quiet Wi-Fi power cycle (itlwm_fast & 1): a user power-off (setPOWER 0)
   stops the card without telling WCL; the following firmware start sends no
   ResetInterface/DriverAvailable. Boot and real failures are reported as
   before; a firmware start that fails after a quiet stop reports
   "unavailable". System sleep is never quiet: a priority sleep/wake
   notification marks the sleep, the card then stops and reports exactly as
   in 7204c69, and a Wi-Fi that was quietly off is reported unavailable at
   that moment. If the notification cannot be registered, part 1 is off.
2. Hold requests while the firmware loads (itlwm_fast & 2): a WCL scan or join
   that arrives between power-on (or a MAC-change restart) and firmware ready
   is kept instead of failing with kIOReturnNotReady. iwx_init() starts its
   first scan with the held scan's channels and SSID; a held join resumes at
   READY.
3. Fast join (itlwm_fast & 4): a join restricts the next scan to the BSS's
   channel and SSID, and a full background scan already running is ended
   through an asynchronous UMAC scan abort, so ieee80211_end_scan() picks the
   BSS now instead of after up to 3.8 s (#40). After the join's own scan,
   scanning covers all channels again.

Changes from the 1st version: the 1st version made system sleep quiet as
well; on the tester's Mac (AX210, macOS 26.7.3) the Mac then woke again 1-2 s
after going to sleep. Sleep and wake now behave as in 7204c69 (part 1 above).
Build fix 1: AirportItlwmV2.cpp includes <IOKit/pwr_mgt/RootDomain.h>, which
declares registerPrioritySleepWakeInterest (first Actions build of the 2nd
version failed with "use of undeclared identifier").

Boot-arg itlwm_fast=N selects the parts (default 7); itlwm_fast=0 behaves like
7204c69. Only the AIRPORT_WCL (Sequoia/Tahoe) builds and the iwx HAL change.
The 1st version was built by GitHub Actions and tested for Wi-Fi off/on only;
this version is not compiled or run by the author of this patch. Test from a
USB EFI copy and keep the previous AirportItlwm.kext.

